# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Added `@vercel/analytics` (v2.0.1) to project dependencies
- Updated package-lock.json with new dependency tree

### 2. Analytics Integration
- Modified `src/App.tsx` to import and include the Analytics component
- Added `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react";` at the top of the file
- Placed `<Analytics />` component at the end of the App component's JSX, following Vercel's recommended pattern for React/Vite applications

### Implementation Details
The Analytics component was added to the root App component, which ensures it will track page views across all routes in the application. The component is placed at the end of the main div, which is the recommended location according to Vercel's documentation.

### Files Modified
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency resolution
- `src/App.tsx` - Added Analytics component import and usage

### Verification Steps Completed
1. ✅ TypeScript type checking passed (`npm run typecheck`)
2. ✅ Production build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
3. ✅ No type errors or build errors introduced

## Next Steps
After deployment to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics tab → Enable button)
2. Verify analytics are being collected by checking for `/_vercel/insights/*` requests in the browser's Network tab
3. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard after user visits accumulate

## Framework-Specific Notes
This implementation follows the React/Vite-specific instructions from the official Vercel Analytics documentation. The `@vercel/analytics/react` import is specifically designed for React applications using Vite as the build tool.
